Q22. How do you design for LDV (Large Data Volumes) in Salesforce?What strategies would you use to avoid governor limit exceptions when processing millions of records?
Ans22. If your deployment has tens of thousands of users, tens of millions of records, or hundreds of gigabytes of total record storage, you have a large data volume.
before desigining the solution for large data volume , i will consider the limits and challengea that can arise.
large data volumes(LDV) can lead to sluggish performance, including slower queries, slower search and list views, and slower sandbox refreshing.( real time example
summary by country sceen , Read only screen.

STrategies for LDV:

Mitigating Data Skew
1. Data skew -- Data skew happens when more than 10,000 child records are associated which the same parent record within an org. due to whih reord locking and sharing calculation can take time even the performance of the org can
degrade if not handled. Distribute child records across a pool of dummy/placeholder accounts.
ownership skew: When a large number of records with the same object type are owned by a single user like for integration user.Assign high-volume records to users without a role, or distribute ownership across multiple generic system users.
Lookup skew: Lookup skew happens when a very large number of records are associated with a single record in the lookup object. Distribute lookup lookups across multiple placeholder records; use asynchronous batching to sequence updates.


